.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NQPWENC 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqpwenc ,
.Nm nqpwenc2 ,
.Nm nqpwdec ,
.Nm nqpbkdf2
.Nd keep a secret key under a passphrase
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqpwenc
.Fa "const uint8_t *pw" "size_t pwlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ad" "size_t alen"
.Fa "uint32_t m" "uint32_t t" "uint32_t p"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqpwenc2
.Fa "int kdf"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pw" "size_t pwlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ad" "size_t alen"
.Fa "uint32_t m" "uint32_t t" "uint32_t p"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqpbkdf2
.Fa "nqhalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pw" "size_t pwlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *salt" "size_t slen"
.Fa "uint32_t iters"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqpwdec
.Fa "const uint8_t *pw" "size_t pwlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ad" "size_t alen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *sk" "size_t cap" "size_t *sklen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqpwenc
encrypts the secret key
.Fa sk
(1 to
.Dv NQPWMAX ,
65536, bytes) under the passphrase
.Fa pw
(1 to
.Dv NQPWLEN ,
4096, bytes) in the format noqtis-pwkey-1, and
.Fn nqpwdec
decrypts it.
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1
writes such keys, and
.Xr noqtis-sign 1
and
.Xr noqtis-dec 1
read them, with the key file's first line as
.Fa ad .
.Pp
The format, all numbers big-endian:
.Bl -column "KDF: 1 Argon2id (version 0x13), 2 PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256" "sklen" -offset indent
.It Sy field Ta Sy bytes
.It Li NQPW Ta 4
.It version, 1 Ta 1
.It KDF: 1 Argon2id (version 0x13), 2 PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 Ta 1
.It AEAD, 1: ChaCha20-Poly1305 Ta 1
.It Fa m , No KiB (0 under PBKDF2) Ta 4
.It Fa t , No passes, or PBKDF2 iterations Ta 4
.It Fa p , No lanes (0 under PBKDF2) Ta 4
.It salt, random Ta 16
.It ciphertext of Fa sk Ta Fa sklen
.It tag Ta 16
.El
.Pp
The KDF of the passphrase and the salt, Argon2id
.Pq Xr nqa2id 3
with
.Fa t ,
.Fa m
and
.Fa p ,
or PBKDF2 with
.Fa t
iterations
.Pq see Fn nqpwenc2 ,
gives 44 bytes: the AEAD's key and its nonce.
The associated data is the 35-byte header followed by
.Fa ad
(at most 1024 bytes;
.Dv NULL
with 0 for none), so no field of the header and no byte of
.Fa ad
can change without the tag failing.
The output is
.Fa sklen
+
.Dv NQPWOVH
(51) bytes.
.Pp
.Fa m ,
.Fa t
and
.Fa p
are 0 for the defaults
.Dv NQPWM
(65536 KiB, 64 MiB),
.Dv NQPWT
(3) and
.Dv NQPWP
(4).
.Fn nqpwenc ,
.Fn nqpwenc2
and
.Fn nqpwdec
enforce the same Argon2id limits: memory
.Dv NQPWMMIN
(8 MiB) to
.Dv NQPWMMAX
(1 GiB), 1 to
.Dv NQPWTMAX
(16) passes, 1 to
.Dv NQPWPMAX
(16) lanes, and
.Fa m
\(mu
.Fa t
at most
.Dv NQPWWORK
(4194304, 4 GiB of passes).
.Fn nqpwdec
checks the magic, version, algorithms, parameters and size before it
derives anything, so a file cannot make it take more than 1 GiB or more
than 4 GiB of passes; then a wrong passphrase, a changed byte or
another
.Fa ad
fails the tag.
On any error
.Fa sk
is zeroed, and
.Fn nqpwenc
leaves nothing in
.Fa out .
.Fa sk
and
.Fa out
may not overlap.
.Pp
In symbols, with
.Sy ||
concatenation, BE32 a number in 4 bytes most significant first, S the
16-byte salt, P the passphrase, A the caller's
.Fa ad ,
SK the secret key and kdf the KDF byte:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
H   = "NQPW" || 0x01 || kdf || 0x01
      || BE32(m) || BE32(t) || BE32(p) || S       35 bytes
OKM = Argon2id(P, S, t, m, p, T = 44)             if kdf = 1
      (version 0x13, no secret value K, no associated data X)
OKM = PBKDF2(PRF = HMAC-SHA-256, P, S, c = t, dkLen = 44)
                                                  if kdf = 2, m = p = 0
K   = OKM[0..31],  N = OKM[32..43]
out = H || ChaCha20-Poly1305(K, N, H || A, SK)
.Ed
.Pp
Argon2id is that of RFC 9106 section 3 with t passes over m KiB in p
lanes and a 44-byte tag; PBKDF2 is that of RFC 8018 section 5.2 with
HMAC-SHA-256 as its PRF; ChaCha20-Poly1305 is that of RFC 8439
section 2.8, with associated data H || A, its output the ciphertext then
the 16-byte tag.
PBKDF2 with c iterations, for block i = 1, 2, ...:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
U_1 = HMAC(P, S || BE32(i));  U_j = HMAC(P, U_(j-1))
T_i = U_1 xor U_2 xor ... xor U_c
DK  = first dkLen bytes of T_1 || T_2 || ...
.Ed
.Pp
A new salt makes a new key and nonce for each call, so the nonce is
never used twice with one key.
.Pp
.Fn nqpwenc2
is
.Fn nqpwenc
with the derivation chosen by
.Fa kdf :
.Dv NQPWA2 ,
Argon2id as above and the default everywhere, or
.Dv NQPWPB ,
PBKDF2 with HMAC-SHA-256 (RFC 8018 section 5.2) for places whose rules
ask for it.
Under
.Dv NQPWPB
the header's KDF byte is 2,
.Fa t
is the iteration count (0 for
.Dv NQPWI ,
600000; from
.Dv NQPWIMIN ,
100000, to
.Dv NQPWIMAX ,
10000000),
.Fa m
and
.Fa p
are 0, and OKM is the 44 bytes PBKDF2 gives for the passphrase and the
salt.
.Fn nqpwdec
reads both; the KDF byte is in H, so the tag covers it.
.Pp
.Fn nqpbkdf2
is PBKDF2 itself on the HMAC of
.Fa alg
.Pq Xr nqhash 3 ,
a SHA-2 or SHA-3 hash
.Pf ( Dv NQS224
to
.Dv NQS3512 ;
not SHAKE):
.Fa outlen
bytes (1 to
.Dv NQPBOMAX ,
1024) after
.Fa iters
iterations (1 to
.Dv NQPBIMAX ,
100000000).
It costs an attacker no memory, which Argon2id does.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Each function returns
.Dv NQOK ,
or
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Bq Er NQEARG
A passphrase that is empty or too long, an
.Fa ad
over 1024 bytes, a key that is empty or too long, parameters outside
the limits (for
.Fn nqpwenc
and
.Fn nqpwenc2 ) ,
a
.Fa kdf
other than
.Dv NQPWA2
and
.Dv NQPWPB
.Pq for Fn nqpwenc2 ,
an
.Fa outlen
or
.Fa iters
outside its limits
.Pq for Fn nqpbkdf2 ,
or a
.Dv NULL
pointer (for
.Fn nqpbkdf2 :
.Fa out ,
or
.Fa pw
or
.Fa salt
given with a length).
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
.Fa alg
is SHAKE
.Pq Fn nqpbkdf2 .
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa cap
is too small;
.Pf * Fa outlen
or
.Pf * Fa sklen
gets the size needed.
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
.Fn nqpwdec :
.Fa in
is not noqtis-pwkey-1 (magic, version, KDF or AEAD), or is too short.
.It Bq Er NQELIM
.Fn nqpwdec :
.Fa in
asks for parameters outside the limits, or holds a key over
.Dv NQPWMAX .
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
.Fn nqpwdec :
the passphrase is wrong, or a byte of
.Fa in
or
.Fa ad
differs.
.It Bq Er NQEMEM
Argon2id's memory could not be allocated.
.It Bq Er NQERNG
.Fn nqpwenc
or
.Fn nqpwenc2 :
the salt could not be drawn.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A secret key
.Fa sk
of
.Fa sklen
bytes (at most 4096 here) under a passphrase, with the default
parameters, and back:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint8_t file[4096 + NQPWOVH], back[4096];
const char *pw = "correct horse battery staple";
size_t n, k;
int rc = nqpwenc((const uint8_t *)pw, strlen(pw), NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0,
                 sk, sklen, file, sizeof file, &n);

if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqpwdec((const uint8_t *)pw, strlen(pw), NULL, 0, file, n,
               back, sizeof back, &k);
/* back holds the k bytes of sk; NQEVRFY for another passphrase */
nqwipe(back, sizeof back);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqa2id 3 ,
.Xr nqhash 3
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 9106 (Argon2id), RFC 8439 (ChaCha20-Poly1305), RFC 8018 (PBKDF2).
